DATASET ATTRIBUTIONS

The `datasets/` package bundles small example time series for testing and
documentation. The data values are factual measurements from public/
government sources and are not subject to copyright (per Feist v Rural
Telephone Service Co., 499 U.S. 340 (1991), which held that compilations of
factual data lack the originality required for copyright). The Go encoding
of these values is MIT-licensed under this LICENSE.

Specific source attributions per dataset are in each `datasets/*.go` file
header. Summary:

  AirPassengers  Box & Jenkins (1976), originally TWA airline statistics.
                 Public-domain factual data (>30 years old).
  Wineind        Australian Bureau of Statistics, monthly wine sales.
                 Per ABS (cc-by-4.0): "ABS data may be used, reproduced,
                 published [...] freely". Mirrors pmdarima version (MIT).
  Lynx           MacKenzie River Hudson's Bay Company trapping records,
                 1821-1934. Public domain (>100 years old).
  Austres        Australian Bureau of Statistics, quarterly residents.
                 Public ABS data; mirrors R's stats::austres.
  Sunspots       SIDC / Royal Observatory Belgium. Public scientific data.
  Woolyrnq       Australian Bureau of Statistics, quarterly wool yarn.
                 Public ABS data.
  Ausbeer        Australian Bureau of Statistics, quarterly beer production.
                 Public ABS data; mirrors pmdarima version (MIT). The
                 longer R::forecast version (218 obs through Q2 2010) is
                 fetched on-demand via tools/fetch_datasets/.
  Heartrate      MIT-BIH database / PhysioNet. Open data per ODC-by license.
  Taylor         UK National Grid, half-hourly electricity demand.
                 Open Government Licence (UK) v3.0.
  Gasoline       US Energy Information Administration, weekly motor
                 gasoline product supplied. US government work, public
                 domain (17 USC 105). Mirrors pmdarima version. The longer
                 R::forecast version is fetched on-demand via
                 tools/fetch_datasets/.
  WWWusage       Makridakis et al. (1998), classic forecasting textbook.
                 Republished in many open educational sources.
  Msft           Yahoo Finance historical pricing. Factual market data.
